/**
 * E2E: Fetching a single comment's details by comment ID for a given post.
 *
 * Business Workflow:
 * 1. Register a new user, who will author the comment.
 * 2. Register a new post (to comment on), owned by that user.
 * 3. Add a comment to the post by its ID, using the user's account.
 * 4. Retrieve the comment details by its comment ID and parent post ID — verify all expected fields are present and correct (content, author, timestamps, parent, relations).
 * 5. Attempt to fetch a comment with a non-existent ID (random UUID) and expect a not-found error.
 * 6. Register another user account, log in as this user (to simulate a public/other user), and fetch the same comment ID — expect access (since comments are public) and check returned details are as expected.
